{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448122-the-benefits-of-draining-a-human-dry","id":1448122,"title":"The benefits of draining a human dry","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-10T07:05:09-07:00","id":1448122,"title":"The benefits of draining a human dry","content":"Currently the only benefit to draining a human dry is getting rid of your last hunger. That doesn't seem to jive with the movies/novels, where vampires go from torpored and badly damaged to perfectly healthy by draining some poor schlub dry. So how about this: draining a human dry heals two aggs. No rouse check, no willpower point; you suck a human to death and you just check off two aggs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T08:17:44-07:00","id":1448126,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Healing an additional point of Agg without willpower expenditure when draining a guy dry might be a good idea for V20. But I'm also on the fence because, well, lying low while you recover from your wounds makes for an interesting manhunt, and if you can just undo that part by making bodies real fast I feel a lot is lost from the manhunt. Since you're talking V5, maybe you could restore the way bloodbuffs often worked in V20 and have it so that after draining a mortal you're JACKED TO THE EYEBALLS ON BLAHD AND READY TO RIP'N TEAHR (Fully buffed up for free)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T08:40:37-07:00","id":1448131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448122-the-benefits-of-draining-a-human-dry#post1448122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currently the only benefit to draining a human dry is getting rid of your last hunger. That doesn't seem to jive with the movies/novels, where vampires go from torpored and badly damaged to perfectly healthy by draining some poor schlub dry. So how about this: draining a human dry heals two aggs. No rouse check, no willpower point; you suck a human to death and you just check off two aggs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it depends on how bad your Hunger is. You can make Rouse checks WHILE drinking I'd rule as an ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T10:03:04-07:00","id":1448137,"title":"","content":"I don\u00b4t like it becuase it goes agaisnt the spirit of aggravated damage wich is damage you cannot regen in combat and theorically can lead to almost infinite battles.<br /> <br /> Also the idea of a vampire hiding to lick their wounds after a serious battle is a very useful theme for plot hooks.<br /> <br /> Why not replace it with another bonus like recovering willpower becuase the beast feels good killing? It fits thematically and showacases the influence of the beast over the mind of the vampire<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T11:22:21-07:00","id":1448149,"title":"","content":"Recovering WP is a bit of a strange thing because the Beast and the soul are supposed to be seperate spirits so satisfying the beast shouldn't satisfy your spirit... as odd, difficult to articulate and esoteric these ideas are. But I suppose V5 blends the two a bit more so it could work.<br /> <br /> Once you start gaining willpower for overfeeding you gotta ask why you arent getting WP for all feeding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 05-10-2021, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T12:23:56-07:00","id":1448161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448122-the-benefits-of-draining-a-human-dry?p=1448137#post1448137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not replace it with another bonus like recovering willpower becuase the beast feels good killing? It fits thematically and showacases the influence of the beast over the mind of the vampire</div> </div> </div> </div>This is *exactly* the homebrew rule that I use; I also give the vampire two &quot;virtual&quot; blood points (above and beyond their capacity if they are already full) that can be spent that evening.<br /> <br /> I want the temptations of killing to be very present and very real... it's the same philosophy that underlies my making Frenzy so much more full of benefits. Come on... let the monster out to play. He gets lots of bonus dice....<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T22:41:28-07:00","id":1448199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Legendre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448122-the-benefits-of-draining-a-human-dry?p=1448161#post1448161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is *exactly* the homebrew rule that I use; I also give the vampire two &quot;virtual&quot; blood points (above and beyond their capacity if they are already full) that can be spent that evening.<br /> <br /> I want the temptations of killing to be very present and very real... it's the same philosophy that underlies my making Frenzy so much more full of benefits. Come on... let the monster out to play. He gets lots of bonus dice....<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Bright minds really think alike<br /> <br /> In my games frenzy is the main degeneration cause , you let the beast take control and it keep some of it.<br /> <br /> In combat it doubles regeneration and lets the player ignore penalties from injuries so if they feel &quot;like ridding the beast&quot; they can take more damage and get a second wind but they don\u00b4t get any dice bonus as I feel that would make frenzy mandatory instead of a small buff that can change the tide of the battle between fighters of equal level.<br /> <br /> However some clans and bloodlines do get a bonus while in frenzy becuase they have clan gifts that help them be more unique example the brujah (Fire of Carthage) deal agravated damage against lower blood potency enemies while in frenzy and the gangrel become into werebats (Licantropy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T10:19:44-07:00","id":1448237,"title":"","content":"Empty juice boxes are easier to throw away","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19506-killtron","name":"Killtron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}